<title>GERMANY: BASF invests in Chinese fibres plant.</title>
<headline>BASF invests in Chinese fibres plant.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAVEN, Germany 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's BASF AG said on Thursday that together with partner  China Worldbest Group Corp it had agreed to build a plant in China for the production of carpet fibres.</p>
<p>BASF said the investment in the facility would be around $100 million, with BASF taking up 70 percent of the shares in a newly-formed joint venture company set to run the plant.</p>
<p>The new factory, to be based near Shanghai, is due to start production in the last quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>In its first phase, production capacity is estimated at around 7,000 tonnes of the Nylon 6 material each year, rising to 19,000 tonnes, BASF said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
